{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Player-Avatar Relationship.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Player-Avatar Relationship.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"player avatar relationship player avatar relationship","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Player-Avatar Relationship.md","fileName":"Player-Avatar Relationship.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Player-Avatar Relationship","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-18 16:43\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Character and Interactive Story Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Character and Interactive Story Design","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Player-Avatar Relationship.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Player-Avatar Relationship.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"player avatar relationship player avatar relationship","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Player-Avatar Relationship.md","fileName":"Player-Avatar Relationship.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Player-Avatar Relationship","heading":"Player-Avatar Relationship","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The player-avatar relationship is the psychological and mechanical connection between a player and the character representing them. A blank or customizable avatar encourages projection, while a strongly authored protagonist asks the player to guide a distinct personality.\n\nThe relationship should match the game's story and control. Forcing choices that contradict an established character or withholding actions implied by the role can make the player feel detached from both avatar and plot.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Character and Interactive Story Design","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Player-Avatar Relationship.md::2","sourceKe